        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: небо",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "небо (nébo) — \"the sky\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "небо (nébo) — borrowed from Church Slavonic, says Vasmer; the native East Slavic form is нёбо, now \"the palate\". Both go back to Proto-Slavic nebo, a cousin of Sanskrit nábhas, \"mist, sky\", Greek néphos, \"cloud\", and Latin nebula, \"mist\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
