              "text": "солнце (sólntse) from Proto-Slavic sŭlnĭce, a diminutive of sŭlnĭ, \"sun\", built like сердце, \"heart\" (Vasmer). Vasmer lists Lithuanian sáulė, \"sun\", and Sanskrit svar, \"sun, light\"; Latin sōl and English sun go back to the same PIE word."
